# Prompt History — During-Task Reminder

## When This Rule Applies
After every task completion, when Cursor stops and requests developer review.

## What To Do
At the end of every task summary (after changes, decisions, and security/performance notes),
append the following prompt log notice:

```
---
> **Prompt log:** This prompt will be captured in the sprint log when the Quality Gate passes.
> Meaningful: [Yes / No — reason]
> Response summary: [One sentence — the concrete artifact or decision the AI produced this turn]
---
```

Set **Meaningful: Yes** if the prompt that triggered this task:
- Contains a task instruction or task ID
- Makes an architectural or design decision
- Iterates on a previous AI output with feedback
- Rejects or modifies AI-generated content
- Contains a role persona ("You are acting as...")
- Is longer than one sentence with specific direction

Set **Meaningful: No** if the prompt was:
- A single continuation word only (proceed, yes, ok, approved)
- A status check with no new instruction
- An acknowledgement with no decision

**Response summary rules:**
- One factual sentence, past tense (e.g., "Generated TicketRepository interface with 6 methods")
- Name the concrete artifact; if Meaningful is No, write "N/A — no substantive output"

## Sprint Boundary Reminder
When a sprint Quality Gate passes, add before closing the sprint:

```
---
> **Sprint log:** Now creating prompt-history/sprint-X.X.md from this session's transcript.
> Following the prompt-history-sprint-log rule.
---
```

Then immediately apply the prompt-history-sprint-log rule.

## What NOT To Do
- Do not create the sprint log file mid-sprint — only at Quality Gate
- Do not ask the developer to manually copy prompts — Cursor reads the transcript
- Do not include this notice in the sprint log file itself (it is a reminder only)
